From 1ae003fa4ed6a64aa0e9a784b6252c70c732c15e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Krish Paul <me@krishnendu.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 04:55:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Now Playing: level meters and a spectrum that XML layouts can
 show

A layout opts in by naming widgets: vu_left and vu_right for the level
and vu_peak_left and vu_peak_right for a held peak, each an lv_bar or,
for a round dial, an lv_arc; vu_needle_left and vu_needle_right for any
object to be turned with the level like a needle; vu_band_1 to
vu_band_10, with vu_band_peak_ caps, for a spectrum in ten octave bands;
and optionally an object named vu_meter around them so the group leaves
with the controls while the lyrics are open. The player sets the values
on the existing 50 ms player tick; no Lua runs per frame.

The vu_meter group can also be swiped sideways: hidden labels inside it
named vu_swipe_left and vu_swipe_right give the plugin action to run for
each direction, and the group becomes a swipe dead zone for the shell.

The levels are measured where PCM leaves for the output
(audio_output_write, audio_output_write_s24, and the SDL sink on the
host), in short blocks stamped with the time they are heard, so the meter
moves with the sound and not a buffer ahead of it. Local output uses the
ALSA buffer size; the aplay pipe targets use what waits in the pipe plus
an estimate for aplay's buffer and the Bluetooth link. DoP frames are
skipped. Nothing is measured unless a meter asked within the last second,
and the spectrum's ten band-pass filters run only for a layout that
names a band.

New capability token: ui.player_layout_meter.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
